                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "303f599e-5100-3cd3-a4d1-2a130071bce0",
                                        "entry_id": "47820a1a-2c19-304b-9754-c0326882921a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To change gradually."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd68303a-8390-42a9-b23e-abaacaaea8c3",
                                                "sense_id": "303f599e-5100-3cd3-a4d1-2a130071bce0",
                                                "text": "As the species graduate into each other, both in form and in habits, from the grass-eating Geese to the fish-eating Harelds, it is difficult, […] to divide this large group into sections."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd9836ae-e948-4c9b-bc07-f4e6f347b71a",
                                                "sense_id": "303f599e-5100-3cd3-a4d1-2a130071bce0",
                                                "text": "Yadav, born Bharat Kalicharan, was a petty thief who had graduated to bigger crimes, terrorising Kasturba Nagar, on the edge of the city of Nagpur, in Maharashtra, from the 1990s until his death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af9bf9db-d26b-4776-bcc3-1a1ce2684d30",
                                                "sense_id": "303f599e-5100-3cd3-a4d1-2a130071bce0",
                                                "text": "sandstone which graduates into gneiss; carnelian sometimes graduates into quartz"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a73a1a0-5286-3a25-b005-aa7da7dc4e67",
                                        "entry_id": "47820a1a-2c19-304b-9754-c0326882921a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare gradually; to arrange, temper, or modify by degrees or to a certain degree; to determine the degrees of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12a2406d-b7b7-4d8f-850e-f7a80dd44c34",
                                                "sense_id": "9a73a1a0-5286-3a25-b005-aa7da7dc4e67",
                                                "text": "to graduate the heat of an oven"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19f2bc47-a160-4ecf-9f46-794a5e39bb22",
                                                "sense_id": "9a73a1a0-5286-3a25-b005-aa7da7dc4e67",
                                                "text": "Dyers, who advance and graduate their colours with salts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a13ee456-1ad0-39d3-80b2-2790051f0fd1",
                                        "entry_id": "47820a1a-2c19-304b-9754-c0326882921a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bring to a certain degree of consistency, by evaporation, as a fluid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5deeec42-9aa6-3a8c-8577-18e2d47e4413",
                                        "entry_id": "47820a1a-2c19-304b-9754-c0326882921a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To taper, as the tail of certain birds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a36be567-84ce-302e-a59b-61c03fc8868d",
                                        "entry_id": "47820a1a-2c19-304b-9754-c0326882921a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To approve (a feature) for general release."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22eb3163-cbec-4d83-b567-20e168b67b84",
                                                "sense_id": "a36be567-84ce-302e-a59b-61c03fc8868d",
                                                "text": "We have graduated the new machine-learning features and will roll them out tomorrow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffe41338-e4cd-33cc-bc57-35e88896b4f0",
                                        "entry_id": "47820a1a-2c19-304b-9754-c0326882921a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an idol: to exit a group; or of a virtual YouTuber, to leave a management agency; usually accompanied with \\\"graduation ceremony\\\" send-offs, increased focus on the leaving member, and the like."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Japanese",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "073e01e9-d786-436e-9186-40561a49eaa3",
                                                "sense_id": "ffe41338-e4cd-33cc-bc57-35e88896b4f0",
                                                "text": "Fans speculate that she was forced to graduate due to harassment and doxxing by stalkers and haters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
